      "explanation": "Influenza is an enveloped, segmented (8 segments), negative-sense ssRNA orthomyxovirus. Antigenic shift is reassortment of whole segments (HA or NA) between animal and human strains in a co-infected host, often pigs. It produces a new subtype and can cause pandemics. Antigenic drift is gradual point mutations in HA and NA, causing seasonal epidemics, which is why the vaccine is updated every year. Hemagglutinin binds sialic acid for entry, and neuraminidase releases new virions.",
