      "topic": "Segmented RNA viruses",
      "stem": "Which group lists only viruses with segmented genomes?",
      "options": {
        "A": "Retrovirus, coronavirus, togavirus",
        "B": "Hepadnavirus, herpesvirus, poxvirus",
        "C": "Picornavirus, calicivirus, and flavivirus",
        "D": "Bunyavirus, influenza, arenavirus, rotavirus",
        "E": "Paramyxovirus, rhabdovirus, filovirus"
      },
      "answer": "D",
      "explanation": "Segmented RNA viruses ('BOARs'): Bunyaviruses, Orthomyxoviruses, Arenaviruses (LCMV, Lassa fever), and Reoviruses. Segmentation allows reassortment, which is the basis of influenza antigenic shift. Negative-sense ssRNA viruses must bring their own RNA-dependent RNA polymerase. Their naked genome is not infectious, while positive-sense genomes can serve directly as mRNA.",
