      "explanation": "Hookworms (Necator americanus, Ancylostoma duodenale) penetrate the skin of bare feet (ground itch), migrate through the lungs, and attach to the small intestine, where they feed on blood. This causes iron deficiency anemia. Treat with albendazole or mebendazole plus iron. Diphyllobothrium latum causes B12 deficiency. Dog and cat hookworm larvae cause cutaneous larva migrans, a creeping eruption.",
