      "answer": "E",
      "explanation": "De-escalation to the narrowest effective agent once culture results are known reduces C. difficile infection, resistance, and drug toxicity without worsening outcomes. It is a core principle of antimicrobial stewardship. Stopping entirely before an adequate course risks relapse, and oral vancomycin is not absorbed.",
