      "explanation": "Vertical HCV transmission occurs in roughly 5-6% of pregnancies and is higher with HIV co-infection or high viral load. Cesarean delivery is not recommended, and breastfeeding is safe unless nipples are cracked and bleeding. Direct-acting antivirals are generally deferred until after pregnancy pending more safety data; ribavirin is teratogenic and contraindicated. Infants are tested after 18 months or by HCV RNA earlier.",
